If P is plaintext and K the generated bytes, C=P XOR K and
(C XOR K)=P. This identity explains decryption, but a wrong keystream
implementation could still round-trip. Published full-byte vectors and the
independent native oracle therefore test more than self-inversion. Likewise,
a changed ciphertext bit produces the same changed plaintext bit; raw ChaCha20
has no authentication tag. The separate ChaCha20-Poly1305 construction in the
RFC supplies authentication; this API implements the stream-XOR primitive.

> Preserve the 4 KiB histogram, with a constant-byte control

The original input is 64 consecutive keystream blocks at counters zero through
63, using the block-test key and nonce. Encrypting 4,096 zero bytes produces
that same stream. Native byte_histogram() groups values by high nibble into
sixteen bins, each representing sixteen possible byte values. These are not
256 individually displayed frequencies.

Every 4,096-byte input has mean bin count 4096/16=256, including a constant
zero string. That mean cannot test uniformity. Under an ideal independent
uniform-byte model each group has expected count 256; observed deviations are
a finite-sample description, not a proof of randomness, unpredictability,
cipher security or timing behavior.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/chacha20_histogram.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::array<std::uint8_t,32> key{};std::iota(key.begin(),key.end(),std::uint8_t{0});
  const std::array<std::uint8_t,12> nonce{0,0,0,9,0,0,0,0x4a,0,0,0,0};
  const auto stream=dm::algorithms::chacha20_encrypt(key,0,nonce,std::string(4096,'\0'));
  const auto counts=dm::algorithms::byte_histogram(stream,16);
  const auto constant=dm::algorithms::byte_histogram(std::string(4096,'\0'),16);
  const auto total=std::accumulate(counts.begin(),counts.end(),std::size_t{0});
  const auto constant_total=std::accumulate(constant.begin(),constant.end(),std::size_t{0});
  const auto individual=dm::algorithms::byte_histogram(stream);
  if(total!=4096 || constant[0]!=4096) return 1;
  std::vector<double> heights(counts.begin(),counts.end());std::vector<std::string> labels;
  std::print("| high nibble | keystream count | constant-zero count |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t bin=0;bin<16;++bin) {
    labels.push_back(std::format("{:x}",bin));std::print("| {:x} | {} | {} |\n",bin,counts[bin],constant[bin]);
  }
  std::print("\nSample group mean: {}; constant-zero group mean: {}.\n",total/16,constant_total/16);
  std::print("Observed distinct individual byte values: {} out of 256.\n",std::count_if(individual.begin(),individual.end(),[](auto n){return n!=0;}));
  dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(heights,labels,"keystream",dm::RGB{37,99,235})
      .abline_h(256,{220,38,38},1.5).title("4096 keystream bytes: sixteen value groups")
      .x_label("byte group (high nibble)").y_label("observed byte count")
      .y_limits(0,static_cast<double>(*std::max_element(counts.begin(),counts.end()))+100)
      .save_svg("build/chacha20_histogram.svg");
}
```
